    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0231" n="135" xml:id="pg135"/>

                <head>No. 83.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Low</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 21,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your No. 130, of 5th of
                    February, inclosing a copy of a correspondence between yourself and Viceroy Li
                    Hung Chang, upon the subject of sending to the United States a number of Chinese
                    youths to be educated, I have to request you to inform the viceroy that I will
                    gladly render such counsel and advice in the matter as may be in my power.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
